module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.HomogeneousLocalization

/-!
# Ring maps out of the degree-zero localization `A_{(f)}`

Let `A = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒜 n` be a graded ring and let `f ∈ 𝒜 d` with `d > 0`. The degree-zero part

  `A_{(f)} = HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f`

of the localization `A_f` is the ring of sections of the structure sheaf on the projective
standard open `D₊(f) ⊆ Proj 𝒜`, so a morphism of schemes into `D₊(f)` is, after passing to
global sections, a ring map out of `A_{(f)}`. Mathlib constructs `A_{(f)}` as a quotient of the
homogeneous fractions `HomogeneousLocalization.NumDenSameDeg` and supplies the constructor
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk`, the fraction `a / f ^ n` for `a` homogeneous of degree `n • d`,
together with its surjectivity; what it does not supply is a way to define a ring map *out* of
`A_{(f)}`. This file supplies one.

The data needed is exactly what the fraction `a / f ^ n` suggests: a degreewise additive map
`c n : 𝒜 (n * d) →+ P`, multiplicative across degrees, unital, and sending `f` to `1`. Such a
family is `Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios`, and
`Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios.lift` is the induced ring map, characterized by

  `lift (Away.mk 𝒜 hf n a ha) = c n a`.

This is the algebraic half of step 1 of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 01N8]: there `A = S`, `P` is the
ring of sections of `𝒪_Y` over the nonvanishing locus of `ψ(f)`, and `c n` is the map
`a ↦ ψ(a) / ψ(f) ^ n` obtained from the trivialization of an invertible sheaf by a nonvanishing
section.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios`: the degreewise data of a ring map out of `A_{(f)}` —
  a family `c n : 𝒜 (n * d) →+ P` that is unital, multiplicative across degrees, and sends the
  element `f` of degree `d` to `1`.
* `Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios.extend`: that family read on an arbitrary degree,
  which is the function the quotient map is lifted from.
* `Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios.lift`: **the ring map `A_{(f)} →+* P` it induces.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios.lift_mk`: **the characterization.** On the fraction
  `a / f ^ n` the induced map is `c n a`. Together with
  `Stacks.ProjGlobalSectionsAppTop.away_ringHom_ext` — two ring maps out of `A_{(f)}` agreeing on
  every such fraction are equal — this determines `lift` completely.
* `Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios.apply_pow`: the family sends `f ^ n`, of degree
  `n * d`, to `1`. This is the computation that makes the induced map well defined.
* `Stacks.MorphismToProj.HomogeneousRatios.extend_pow_mul`: a power of `f` may be cancelled from
  a product. Both the additivity and the multiplicativity of `lift` reduce to this.

## Implementation notes

**Why the degree of the denominator has to be pinned.** A general
`NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f)` carries a degree `p.deg`, a numerator and a denominator
both in `𝒜 p.deg`, and the only link to `f` is that the denominator lies in the submonoid
generated by `f`. So the denominator is `f ^ i` for some `i`, but nothing in the data says
`p.deg = i * d`. It is forced as soon as `f ^ i ≠ 0`, because distinct graded pieces of a graded
ring meet in `0` (`DirectSum.degree_eq_of_mem_mem`), and `f ^ i = 0` puts `0` in the submonoid,
which makes `A_{(f)}` the zero ring. The latter case is not excluded by hypothesis but discharged:
`HomogeneousRatios.subsingleton_of_zero_mem` shows the *target* `P` is then the zero ring too,
because `1 = c n (f ^ n) = c n 0 = 0` in it. So every proof below splits on
`(0 : A) ∈ Submonoid.powers f` and the degenerate branch is `Subsingleton.elim`. This is the same
case analysis Mathlib performs in `HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk_surjective`.

**The structure fields carry the element and an equation, not a membership proof.** A field spelled
`c 0 ⟨1, _⟩ = 1` would force every user to produce the proof `(1 : A) ∈ 𝒜 (0 * d)` in the exact
form the field expects, and `0 * d` is not definitionally `0` for a variable `d` — `Nat.mul`
recurses on its second argument, so neither `0 * d` nor `1 * d` reduces. The fields are therefore
quantified over an element of the graded piece together with an equation identifying its
underlying element, which is both easier to supply and easier to apply; `toFun_congr` is the same
move for the index that is already fixed.

**`extend` is total, and defined without a `dite` on divisibility.** The function lifted to the
quotient is `p ↦ extend p.deg p.num`, where `extend n : 𝒜 n →+ P` is `c (n / d)` precomposed with
the degree `n / d * d` component of the decomposition of `A`. On a degree of the form `k * d` the
component map is the identity on `𝒜 (k * d)` by `DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same`, so nothing is
lost; on any other degree the value is irrelevant. Defining it this way rather than by cases on
`d ∣ n` keeps the single index transport `k * d / d = k` as the only transport in the file, and it
is isolated in `extend_apply_of_eq`. No existential is unpacked in the *definition*, so the
quotient map needs no `Classical.choose` and the denominator is analysed only in proofs.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N8)
-/

@[expose] public section

open HomogeneousLocalization

namespace Stacks.MorphismToProj

universe u v w

variable {σ : Type w} {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]

/-! ### The degreewise data -/

/-- **The degreewise data of a ring map out of `A_{(f)}`.** For `f` homogeneous of degree `d`, a
family of additive maps `c n : 𝒜 (n * d) →+ P`, one for each `n`, which is unital, multiplicative
across degrees, and sends `f` itself to `1`. Reading `c n a` as the value of the fraction
`a / f ^ n`, the three conditions say that `1 / f ^ 0`, a product of two fractions, and `f / f` go
where they must. -/
structure HomogeneousRatios (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] {d : ℕ} {f : A} (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d)
    (P : Type v) [CommRing P] where
  /-- The value of the fraction `a / f ^ n`, for `a` homogeneous of degree `n * d`. -/
  toFun : ∀ n : ℕ, 𝒜 (n * d) →+ P
  /-- The fraction `1 / f ^ 0` is the unit. -/
  map_one : ∀ a : 𝒜 (0 * d), (a : A) = 1 → toFun 0 a = 1
  /-- Fractions multiply: `(a / f ^ n) · (b / f ^ m) = a b / f ^ (n + m)`. -/
  map_mul : ∀ (n m : ℕ) (a : 𝒜 (n * d)) (b : 𝒜 (m * d)) (ab : 𝒜 ((n + m) * d)),
    (ab : A) = (a : A) * (b : A) → toFun (n + m) ab = toFun n a * toFun m b
  /-- The fraction `f / f` is the unit. -/
  map_den : ∀ a : 𝒜 (1 * d), (a : A) = f → toFun 1 a = 1

namespace HomogeneousRatios

variable {𝒜 : ℕ → σ} [GradedRing 𝒜] {d : ℕ} {f : A} {hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d}
  {P : Type v} [CommRing P]

/-- A power of `f` is homogeneous of degree `n * d`. -/
theorem pow_mem (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d) (n : ℕ) : (f : A) ^ n ∈ 𝒜 (n * d) := by
  simpa [smul_eq_mul, Nat.mul_comm] using SetLike.pow_mem_graded n hf

variable (R : HomogeneousRatios 𝒜 hf P)

/-- The data sees a homogeneous element only through its underlying element: at a fixed index the
value does not depend on the membership proof carried alongside. -/
theorem toFun_congr {n : ℕ} (a b : 𝒜 (n * d)) (h : (a : A) = (b : A)) :
    R.toFun n a = R.toFun n b := by
  rw [Subtype.ext h]

/-- The data sees a homogeneous element only through its underlying element and its index: at two
indices known to be equal the values agree. -/
theorem toFun_cast {n m : ℕ} (h : n = m) (a : 𝒜 (n * d)) (b : 𝒜 (m * d))
    (hab : (a : A) = (b : A)) : R.toFun n a = R.toFun m b := by
  subst h
  exact R.toFun_congr a b hab

/-- **The family sends `f ^ n` to `1`.** This is the computation that makes the lift below well
defined: the denominator of a homogeneous fraction contributes nothing to its value. -/
theorem apply_pow (n : ℕ) (a : 𝒜 (n * d)) (ha : (a : A) = f ^ n) :
    R.toFun n a = 1 := by
  induction n with
  | zero => exact R.map_one a (by simpa using ha)
  | succ k ih =>
      have hf1 : (f : A) ∈ 𝒜 (1 * d) := by simpa using hf
      rw [R.map_mul k 1 ⟨(f : A) ^ k, pow_mem hf k⟩ ⟨f, hf1⟩ a (by rw [ha]; ring),
        ih ⟨(f : A) ^ k, pow_mem hf k⟩ rfl, R.map_den ⟨f, hf1⟩ rfl, one_mul]

/-- **If `0` is a power of `f` then the target is the zero ring.** The family sends `f ^ n` to `1`
and `0` to `0`, so `f ^ n = 0` forces `1 = 0` in `P`. This is what makes the lift below total
without a hypothesis excluding a nilpotent `f`. -/
theorem subsingleton_of_zero_mem (R : HomogeneousRatios 𝒜 hf P)
    (hzero : (0 : A) ∈ Submonoid.powers f) : Subsingleton P := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hzero
  have hmem : (0 : A) ∈ 𝒜 (n * d) := zero_mem _
  have h1 : R.toFun n ⟨(0 : A), hmem⟩ = 1 := R.apply_pow n ⟨(0 : A), hmem⟩ hn.symm
  have h0 : R.toFun n ⟨(0 : A), hmem⟩ = 0 := by
    rw [show (⟨(0 : A), hmem⟩ : 𝒜 (n * d)) = 0 from rfl, map_zero]
  have h10 : (1 : P) = 0 := h1 ▸ h0
  exact subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun y => by rw [← one_mul y, h10, zero_mul]

/-! ### The family read on an arbitrary degree -/

/-- The degree `m` component of an element of `A`, as an additive map into the graded piece. -/
noncomputable def component (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] (m : ℕ) : A →+ 𝒜 m :=
  AddMonoidHom.mk' (fun x => (DirectSum.decompose 𝒜 x) m) (fun x y => by
    rw [DirectSum.decompose_add]
    rfl)

/-- The degree `m` component of an element of degree `m` is the element itself. -/
@[simp] theorem component_apply_of_mem {m : ℕ} {x : A} (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 m) :
    (component 𝒜 m x : A) = x := by
  rw [component, AddMonoidHom.mk'_apply, DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same 𝒜 hx]

/-- **The family `R` read on an arbitrary degree `n`**: the degree `n / d * d` component of the
underlying element, fed to `R.toFun (n / d)`. On a degree of the form `k * d` this is `R.toFun k`
(`extend_apply`); on any other degree its value is irrelevant, and the lift below is
`p ↦ extend p.deg p.num`. -/
noncomputable def extend {n : ℕ} : 𝒜 n →+ P :=
  (R.toFun (n / d)).comp ((component 𝒜 (n / d * d)).comp (AddSubmonoidClass.subtype (𝒜 n)))

/-- **The family on a degree given as a multiple of `d` by an equation.** This is the form in
which `extend` is always used; it carries the file's only index transport. -/
theorem extend_apply_of_eq (hd : 0 < d) {n k : ℕ} (h : n = k * d) (a : 𝒜 n)
    (b : 𝒜 (k * d)) (hab : (a : A) = (b : A)) : R.extend a = R.toFun k b := by
  subst h
  refine R.toFun_cast (Nat.mul_div_cancel k hd) (component 𝒜 (k * d / d * d) (a : A)) b ?_
  rw [component_apply_of_mem (by rw [Nat.mul_div_cancel k hd]; exact a.2), hab]

/-- On a degree of the form `k * d` the family is `R.toFun k`. -/
theorem extend_apply (hd : 0 < d) (k : ℕ) (a b : 𝒜 (k * d))
    (hab : (a : A) = (b : A)) : R.extend a = R.toFun k b :=
  R.extend_apply_of_eq hd rfl a b hab

/-- The family read at two degrees known to be equal, on elements with the same underlying
element, gives the same value. -/
theorem extend_eq_of_eq {n m : ℕ} (h : n = m) (a : 𝒜 n) (b : 𝒜 m)
    (hab : (a : A) = (b : A)) : R.extend a = R.extend b := by
  subst h
  rw [Subtype.ext hab]

/-- **A power of `f` cancels from a product.** The additivity and the multiplicativity of the lift
below both reduce to this. -/
theorem extend_pow_mul (hd : 0 < d) (i k : ℕ) (a : 𝒜 (k * d)) {n : ℕ}
    (hn : n = (i + k) * d) (x : 𝒜 n) (hx : (x : A) = (f : A) ^ i * (a : A)) :
    R.extend x = R.toFun k a := by
  have hmem : (x : A) ∈ 𝒜 ((i + k) * d) := hn ▸ x.2
  rw [R.extend_apply_of_eq hd hn x ⟨(x : A), hmem⟩ rfl,
    R.map_mul i k ⟨(f : A) ^ i, pow_mem hf i⟩ a ⟨(x : A), hmem⟩ hx,
    R.apply_pow i ⟨(f : A) ^ i, pow_mem hf i⟩ rfl, one_mul]

/-- The family is multiplicative across degrees that are multiples of `d`. -/
theorem extend_mul (hd : 0 < d) (k l : ℕ) (a : 𝒜 (k * d)) (b : 𝒜 (l * d))
    (ab : 𝒜 (k * d + l * d)) (hab : (ab : A) = (a : A) * (b : A)) :
    R.extend ab = R.extend a * R.extend b := by
  have hsum : k * d + l * d = (k + l) * d := (Nat.add_mul k l d).symm
  have hmem : (ab : A) ∈ 𝒜 ((k + l) * d) := hsum ▸ ab.2
  rw [R.extend_apply hd k a a rfl, R.extend_apply hd l b b rfl,
    R.extend_apply_of_eq hd hsum ab ⟨(ab : A), hmem⟩ rfl]
  exact R.map_mul k l a b ⟨(ab : A), hmem⟩ hab

/-! ### The lift -/

/-- The function on homogeneous fractions that the lift is obtained from: the family read at the
recorded degree, evaluated on the numerator. -/
noncomputable def liftAux (p : NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f)) : P :=
  R.extend p.num

/-- The denominator of a homogeneous fraction over `Submonoid.powers f` is a power of `f`, and —
unless that power vanishes — the recorded degree is the degree of that power. -/
theorem exists_den_eq_pow (hf : f ∈ 𝒜 d) (hzero : (0 : A) ∉ Submonoid.powers f)
    (p : NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f)) :
    ∃ i : ℕ, ((p.den : A) = f ^ i) ∧ p.deg = i * d := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := p.den_mem
  have hi' : (f : A) ^ i = (p.den : A) := hi
  refine ⟨i, hi'.symm, DirectSum.degree_eq_of_mem_mem 𝒜 ?_ (pow_mem hf i)
    fun h => hzero ⟨i, h⟩⟩
  rw [hi']
  exact p.den.2

/-- Either the target is the zero ring, or a fraction has denominator `f ^ i`, recorded degree
`i * d` and numerator of degree `i * d`. -/
private theorem subsingleton_or_exists_num_mem (R : HomogeneousRatios 𝒜 hf P)
    (p : NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f)) :
    Subsingleton P ∨
      ∃ i : ℕ, (p.den : A) = f ^ i ∧ p.deg = i * d ∧ (p.num : A) ∈ 𝒜 (i * d) := by
  by_cases hzero : (0 : A) ∈ Submonoid.powers f
  · exact Or.inl (R.subsingleton_of_zero_mem hzero)
  obtain ⟨i, hpi, hpdeg⟩ := exists_den_eq_pow hf hzero p
  exact Or.inr ⟨i, hpi, hpdeg, hpdeg ▸ p.num.2⟩

/-- On a fraction whose recorded degree is `i * d`, the auxiliary function is `R.toFun i` of the
numerator. -/
theorem liftAux_eq (hd : 0 < d) (p : NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f)) {i : ℕ}
    (hdeg : p.deg = i * d) (a : 𝒜 (i * d)) (ha : (a : A) = (p.num : A)) :
    R.liftAux p = R.toFun i a :=
  R.extend_apply_of_eq hd hdeg p.num a ha.symm

/-- **The auxiliary function respects the equivalence** defining `A_{(f)}`: two homogeneous
fractions with the same image in `A_f` have the same value. Clearing denominators turns the
hypothesis into an identity between two homogeneous elements of one and the same degree, and
`extend_pow_mul` discharges the powers of `f` on both sides. -/
theorem liftAux_congr (hd : 0 < d) (p q : NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f))
    (h : NumDenSameDeg.embedding 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f) p
      = NumDenSameDeg.embedding 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f) q) :
    R.liftAux p = R.liftAux q := by
  rcases R.subsingleton_or_exists_num_mem p with _ | ⟨i, hpi, hpdeg, hnum_p⟩
  · exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  rcases R.subsingleton_or_exists_num_mem q with _ | ⟨j, hqj, hqdeg, hnum_q⟩
  · exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  rw [NumDenSameDeg.embedding, NumDenSameDeg.embedding, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff,
    Localization.r_iff_exists] at h
  obtain ⟨cc, hcc⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := cc.2
  have hval : (f : A) ^ (l + j) * (p.num : A) = (f : A) ^ (l + i) * (q.num : A) := by
    rw [pow_add, pow_add]
    simpa only [hl, hpi, hqj, mul_assoc, mul_comm, mul_left_comm] using hcc
  have hmem : ((f : A) ^ (l + j) * (p.num : A)) ∈ 𝒜 ((l + j + i) * d) :=
    (Nat.add_mul (l + j) i d) ▸ SetLike.mul_mem_graded (pow_mem hf (l + j)) hnum_p
  have hmem' : ((f : A) ^ (l + i) * (q.num : A)) ∈ 𝒜 ((l + j + i) * d) :=
    hval ▸ hmem
  rw [R.liftAux_eq hd p hpdeg ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ rfl,
    R.liftAux_eq hd q hqdeg ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ rfl,
    ← R.extend_pow_mul hd (l + j) i ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ (by ring_nf) ⟨_, hmem⟩ rfl,
    ← R.extend_pow_mul hd (l + i) j ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ (by ring_nf) ⟨_, hmem'⟩ rfl]
  exact R.extend_eq_of_eq rfl _ _ hval

/-- **The ring map `A_{(f)} →+* P` determined by a family of homogeneous ratios.** It sends the
fraction `a / f ^ n` to `c n a`; see `lift_mk`. -/
noncomputable def lift (hd : 0 < d) : Away 𝒜 f →+* P where
  toFun := Quotient.lift R.liftAux fun p q h => R.liftAux_congr hd p q h
  map_one' := by
    refine Eq.trans (R.extend_apply_of_eq hd (Nat.zero_mul d).symm
      (1 : NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f)).num ⟨1, ?_⟩ ?_) (R.map_one _ rfl)
    · simpa using SetLike.one_mem_graded 𝒜
    · rfl
  map_mul' := by
    refine Quotient.ind₂ fun p q => ?_
    by_cases hzero : (0 : A) ∈ Submonoid.powers f
    · have := R.subsingleton_of_zero_mem hzero
      exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
    obtain ⟨i, hpi, hpdeg⟩ := exists_den_eq_pow hf hzero p
    obtain ⟨j, hqj, hqdeg⟩ := exists_den_eq_pow hf hzero q
    have hnum_p : (p.num : A) ∈ 𝒜 (i * d) := hpdeg ▸ p.num.2
    have hnum_q : (q.num : A) ∈ 𝒜 (j * d) := hqdeg ▸ q.num.2
    have hmem : ((p.num : A) * (q.num : A)) ∈ 𝒜 (i * d + j * d) :=
      SetLike.mul_mem_graded hnum_p hnum_q
    have hdeg : (p * q).deg = i * d + j * d := by
      rw [NumDenSameDeg.deg_mul, hpdeg, hqdeg]
    have h1 : R.liftAux (p * q) = R.extend (⟨_, hmem⟩ : 𝒜 (i * d + j * d)) :=
      R.extend_eq_of_eq hdeg (p * q).num ⟨_, hmem⟩ rfl
    change R.liftAux (p * q) = R.liftAux p * R.liftAux q
    rw [h1, R.extend_mul hd i j ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ ⟨_, hmem⟩ rfl]
    exact congrArg₂ (· * ·)
      (R.extend_apply hd i ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ rfl |>.trans
        (R.liftAux_eq hd p hpdeg ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ rfl).symm)
      (R.extend_apply hd j ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ rfl |>.trans
        (R.liftAux_eq hd q hqdeg ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ rfl).symm)
  map_zero' := by
    refine Eq.trans (R.extend_apply_of_eq hd (Nat.zero_mul d).symm
      (0 : NumDenSameDeg 𝒜 (Submonoid.powers f)).num (0 : 𝒜 (0 * d)) rfl) ?_
    exact map_zero _
  map_add' := by
    refine Quotient.ind₂ fun p q => ?_
    by_cases hzero : (0 : A) ∈ Submonoid.powers f
    · have := R.subsingleton_of_zero_mem hzero
      exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
    obtain ⟨i, hpi, hpdeg⟩ := exists_den_eq_pow hf hzero p
    obtain ⟨j, hqj, hqdeg⟩ := exists_den_eq_pow hf hzero q
    have hnum_p : (p.num : A) ∈ 𝒜 (i * d) := hpdeg ▸ p.num.2
    have hnum_q : (q.num : A) ∈ 𝒜 (j * d) := hqdeg ▸ q.num.2
    have hcomm : (i + j) * d = (j + i) * d := by ring
    have hmemL : ((f : A) ^ i * (q.num : A)) ∈ 𝒜 ((i + j) * d) :=
      (Nat.add_mul i j d) ▸ SetLike.mul_mem_graded (pow_mem hf i) hnum_q
    have hmemR : ((f : A) ^ j * (p.num : A)) ∈ 𝒜 ((i + j) * d) := by
      rw [hcomm]
      exact (Nat.add_mul j i d) ▸ SetLike.mul_mem_graded (pow_mem hf j) hnum_p
    have hsum : ((p + q).num : A)
        = ((⟨_, hmemL⟩ + ⟨_, hmemR⟩ : 𝒜 ((i + j) * d)) : A) := by
      rw [NumDenSameDeg.num_add, hpi, hqj]
      rfl
    have hdeg : (p + q).deg = (i + j) * d := by
      rw [NumDenSameDeg.deg_add, hpdeg, hqdeg, Nat.add_mul]
    have h1 : R.liftAux (p + q)
        = R.extend (⟨_, hmemL⟩ : 𝒜 ((i + j) * d)) + R.extend (⟨_, hmemR⟩ : 𝒜 ((i + j) * d)) := by
      change R.extend (p + q).num = _
      rw [R.extend_eq_of_eq hdeg (p + q).num (⟨_, hmemL⟩ + ⟨_, hmemR⟩) hsum]
      exact map_add _ _ _
    change R.liftAux (p + q) = R.liftAux p + R.liftAux q
    rw [h1, R.extend_pow_mul hd i j ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ rfl ⟨_, hmemL⟩ rfl,
      R.extend_pow_mul hd j i ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ hcomm ⟨_, hmemR⟩ rfl,
      R.liftAux_eq hd p hpdeg ⟨(p.num : A), hnum_p⟩ rfl,
      R.liftAux_eq hd q hqdeg ⟨(q.num : A), hnum_q⟩ rfl, add_comm]

/-- **The characterization of the lift.** On the fraction `a / f ^ n` the induced ring map is
`c n a`. By `Stacks.ProjGlobalSectionsAppTop.away_ringHom_ext` this determines it. -/
theorem lift_mk (hd : 0 < d) (n : ℕ) (x : A) (hx : x ∈ 𝒜 (n • d)) (a : 𝒜 (n * d))
    (ha : (a : A) = x) : R.lift hd (Away.mk 𝒜 hf n x hx) = R.toFun n a :=
  R.extend_apply_of_eq hd (by simp [smul_eq_mul, Nat.mul_comm]) ⟨x, hx⟩ a ha.symm

end HomogeneousRatios

end Stacks.MorphismToProj

